  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Envelope 2: Provision of Dignified Shelter Solutions to Vulnerable Populations in NWS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM proposes a project providing 875 dignified shelter units to IDPs residing in tents in two IOM-managed camps (out of ten camps established under CERF funding in 2020 &#x2013;frequently referred to as CERF sites). The tents in two camps (Abraz and Kafr Takharim camps) will be fully targeted. The project will also contribute to increasing the resilience and improve the economic situation of IDPs living in these two camps through the provision of cash for work activities for 96 beneficiaries. Cash for work activities will include beneficiary selection, training on the installation of the new dignified shelters, and supporting the installation of the new shelters.</narrative>
  </description>
